  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 10. What `W^perp` actually is: a `lambda_1` selection rule\n\nRunning `analyse` on `[3,1,0] (x) [3,1,0]` gives `dim W = 171` out of 225, so **54** directions are lost -- even though that tensor product contains **no singlet** (`[3,1,0]` has Dynkin labels `(2,1)`, so it is not self-dual). The singlet reading of the `adj (x) adj` result was therefore a coincidence of that case.\n\nThe real structure: `W^perp` is **`gl(3)`-invariant**, and is a sum of *entire* isotypic components. Identifying them by the quadratic Casimir `C_2 = Sum_ij E_ij E_ji`, whose value on the irrep `lam` is `Sum_i lam_i (lam_i + 4 - 2i)`:\n\n| `lamA (x) lamB` | dim | decomposition (`lam`: dim) | visible | invisible |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `[2,1,0]^2` | 64 | `(4,2,0):27, (4,1,1):10, (3,3,0):10, (3,2,1):8 x2, (2,2,2):1` | `lam_1 = 4, 3` | `(2,2,2)` |\n| `[3,1,0]^2` | 225 | `(6,2,0):60, (6,1,1):21, (5,3,0):42, (5,2,1):24 x2, (4,4,0):15, (4,3,1):15 x2, (4,2,2):6, (3,3,2):3` | `lam_1 = 6, 5` | `lam_1 = 4, 3` |\n| `[3,0,0]^2` | 100 | `(6,0,0):28, (5,1,0):35, (4,2,0):27, (3,3,0):10` | `lam_1 = 6, 5` | `lam_1 = 4, 3` |\n| `[2,1,0](x)[1,0,0]` | 24 | `(3,1,0):15, (2,2,0):6, (2,1,1):3` | `lam_1 = 3, 2` | none |\n\nIn every case the split is by the **first row of the Young diagram alone**:\n\n```\nlam is VISIBLE   <=>   lam_1  >=  lamA_1 + lamB_1 - 1\n```\n\ni.e. only the top two levels of the `lam_1` grading survive. Everything below is invisible, whatever its dimension. This is consistent with the mechanism: `<Om(w)|` sits at the top of the `lam_1` grading and a **single** transfer-matrix insertion can lower `lam_1` by at most one step -- which is exactly why products of two `tau`'s recovered the missing direction in §6.\n\nNote `[3,0,0]` is *rectangular* and still loses 37 of 100. So this obstruction is **not** the rectangular-vs-generic distinction; it is a separate, purely `lam_1`-graded effect.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 10a. Irrep content of W and W^perp via the quadratic Casimir. ---- *)\nClearAll[irrepSplit, dimOfLam, c2OfLam, lamTable, lamOfC2, splitByRule];\ndimOfLam[l_] := (l[[1]] - l[[2]] + 1) (l[[2]] - l[[3]] + 1) (l[[1]] - l[[3]] + 2)/2;\nc2OfLam[l_] := Sum[l[[i]] (l[[i]] + 4 - 2 i), {i, 3}];\nlamTable[n_] := lamTable[n] = Select[Flatten[Table[{a, b, n - a - b}, {a, 0, n}, {b, 0, n}], 1], #[[1]] >= #[[2]] >= #[[3]] >= 0 &];\n(* C2 is injective on partitions of fixed size for gl(3), so it labels the irreps *)\nlamOfC2[c_, n_] := lamOfC2[c, n] = First @ Select[lamTable[n], c2OfLam[#] == c &];\n\nirrepSplit[lA_, lB_, nTw_, seed_] := Module[\n  {d = repDim[lA, lB], uP = uPQ, tg, wS, oms, rows, rk, ns, c2, full, piv, M, sub},\n  tg = tagsG[uP];\n  SeedRandom[seed];\n  wS = DeleteDuplicates @ Select[\n     Table[RandomSample[Range[-11, 11] /. 0 -> 12, 3] + {RandomInteger[{1, 5}]/3, RandomInteger[{1, 5}]/4, RandomInteger[{1, 5}]/7}, {nTw}],\n     (Length[Union[#]] == 3 && FreeQ[#, 0]) &];\n  oms = Table[First @ omegaG[lA, lB, 1/3, -8/57, uP][w], {w, wS}];\n  rows = Join @@ Table[prim /@ Table[om.Normal[If[t[[1]] === 0, IdentityMatrix[d, SparseArray],\n       opG[lA, lB, 1/3, -8/57][t[[1]], t[[2]]][t[[3]]]]], {t, tg}], {om, oms}];\n  rk = MatrixRank[rows];\n  ns = If[rk < d, NullSpace[rows], {}];\n  c2 = Normal @ Sum[EtG[lA, lB][i, j].EtG[lA, lB][j, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\n  full = Sort @ Tally[Eigenvalues[c2]];\n  If[ns === {}, sub = {},\n   piv = Flatten[Position[#, 1, 1, 1] & /@ RowReduce[ns]];\n   M = Table[c2.v, {v, ns}][[All, piv]].Inverse[ns[[All, piv]]];\n   sub = Sort @ Tally[Eigenvalues[M]]];\n  <|\"reps\" -> {lA, lB}, \"dim\" -> d, \"nTwists\" -> Length[wS], \"rankW\" -> rk, \"dimWperp\" -> d - rk,\n    \"C2full\" -> full, \"C2Wperp\" -> sub, \"glInvariant\" -> (ns === {} ||\n      MatrixRank[Join[ns, Flatten[Table[Normal[EtG[lA, lB][i, j]].v, {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {v, ns}], 2]]] == Length[ns])|>];\n\n(* the conjectured selection rule: lam is VISIBLE iff lam_1 >= lamA_1 + lamB_1 - 1.\n   Multiplicities are taken from the MEASURED decomposition, so only the split is predicted. *)\nsplitByRule[r_Association] := Module[{lA = r[\"reps\"][[1]], lB = r[\"reps\"][[2]], n, cut, inv},\n  n = Total[lA] + Total[lB];\n  cut = lA[[1]] + lB[[1]] - 2;\n  inv = Select[r[\"C2full\"], lamOfC2[#[[1]], n][[1]] <= cut &];\n  <|\"predictedDimWperp\" -> Total[Last /@ inv],\n    \"predictedInvisibleLams\" -> ({lamOfC2[#[[1]], n], #[[2]]/dimOfLam[lamOfC2[#[[1]], n]], #[[2]]} & /@ inv),\n    \"measuredDimWperp\" -> r[\"dimWperp\"],\n    \"RULE HOLDS\" -> (Total[Last /@ inv] == r[\"dimWperp\"] &&\n       Sort[First /@ inv] == Sort[First /@ r[\"C2Wperp\"]])|>];\nGrid[{{\"helpers defined\", {dimOfLam[{3, 1, 0}], c2OfLam[{2, 2, 2}], lamOfC2[12, 6]}}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"773602\" data-output-id=\"43\" data-out-n=\"100\" data-sub-idx=\"10\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"23\" data-sub-start=\"41\" data-sub-end=\"41\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[100]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGJlZ2lue2FycmF5fXt8Y3xjfH1caGxpbmVcdGV4dHtoZWxwZXJzIGRlZmluZWR9ICYgXGxlZnRcezE1LDEyLFxsZWZ0XHsyLDIsMlxyaWdodFx9XHJpZ2h0XH1cXFxobGluZVxlbmR7YXJyYXl9\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.24em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.89em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:1.2em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">helpers defined</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:1.2em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">12</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:1.2em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.65em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.85em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[100]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{helpers defined} & \\left\\{15,12,\\left\\{2,2,2\\right\\}\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
