  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 11. What fixes it\n\nThree candidate enlargements of the data, all tested on `[3,0,0]^2` (dim 100, `dim W^perp = 37` with one companion insertion).\n\n**(i) More insertions — works.** `<Om(w)| tau(y1,u1) ... tau(yk,uk) |Psi(z)>` reaches\n`lam_1 >= lamA_1 + lamB_1 - k`, so `k = lamA_1 + lamB_1 - lam_1^min` gives complete reconstruction.\nThis is not exotic data: `T_{a,s}(u)` with a larger auxiliary rep is a Cherednik–Bazhanov–Reshetikhin\ndeterminant of the `T_{a,1}`, i.e. exactly a product, so \"the rest of the fusion hierarchy\" is the\nsame fix said invariantly. It is also what FSoV does. The cost is that `k` grows linearly with the\nrep size.\n\n**(ii) A general, non-companion twist `y` — does NOT help.** Replacing the companion `G(y)` by a\nfree `3x3` matrix gives all nine `T_ij(u)` and all nine `2x2` quantum minors, 54 operators instead\nof 32. Every one of them still annihilates the whole 37-dimensional `W^perp`. So the companion\nrestriction is not what limits the reach — a single insertion is.\n\n**(iii) The other polarized vacua — does NOT help.** All six Weyl images `sigma` in `S_3` give a\ngenuine one-dimensional eigen-covector with eigenvalue\n`Lam^sigma_a(w,u) = Sum_{|I|=a} (Prod_{i in I} w_{sigma(i)}) kappa_I(u)` (still closed-form, no Bethe\nequations). But all six, with every single insertion, annihilate the *same* 37-dimensional space.\n\nSo `W^perp` is invisible to the entire **vacuum sector** under one insertion, not merely to the\nhighest-weight vacuum. That is a stronger statement than the `lambda_1` picture suggested, and it\nkills the \"start lower in the grading\" idea: the lowest-weight vacuum buys nothing. **Only more\ninsertions work.**",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 11a. The three candidate fixes, on [3,0,0]^2. ---- *)\nClearAll[lS, dS, wSS, omsS, opS, nsS, nsT, opsGen, vacEigP, omegaP, randTauS];\nlS = {3, 0, 0}; dS = repDim[lS, lS];\nSeedRandom[5150];\nwSS = DeleteDuplicates @ Select[\n   Table[RandomSample[Range[-11, 11] /. 0 -> 12, 3] + {RandomInteger[{1, 5}]/3, RandomInteger[{1, 5}]/4, RandomInteger[{1, 5}]/7}, {20}],\n   (Length[Union[#]] == 3 && FreeQ[#, 0]) &];\nomsS = Table[First @ omegaG[lS, lS, 1/3, -8/57, uPQ][w], {w, wSS}];\nopS = Table[Normal @ If[t[[1]] === 0, IdentityMatrix[dS, SparseArray], opG[lS, lS, 1/3, -8/57][t[[1]], t[[2]]][t[[3]]]], {t, tagsG[uPQ]}];\nrows1S = Join @@ Table[prim /@ Table[om.O, {O, opS}], {om, omsS}];\nnsS = NullSpace[rows1S]; nsT = Transpose[nsS];\n\n(* (i) products of transfer matrices *)\nrandTauS[] := Normal @ tauG[lS, lS, 1/3, -8/57][RandomChoice[{1, 2}],\n   {RandomInteger[{-9, 9}] + 1/3, RandomInteger[{-9, 9}] + 2/7, RandomInteger[{-9, 9}] + 4/9}][\n   RandomChoice[{7/5, -3/2, 11/4, 2/9, -5/7, 101/37, -57/23}]];\nSeedRandom[999];\nrows2S = Table[RandomChoice[omsS].randTauS[].randTauS[], {400}];\nrows3S = Table[RandomChoice[omsS].randTauS[].randTauS[].randTauS[], {400}];\nkLadder = {MatrixRank[rows1S], MatrixRank[Join[rows1S, rows2S]], MatrixRank[Join[rows1S, rows2S, rows3S]]};\n\n(* (ii) general non-companion twist: ALL T_ij and ALL 2x2 quantum minors *)\nopsGen = Join[\n   Flatten[Table[Normal @ qmG[lS, lS, 1/3, -8/57][{i}, {k}][y], {i, 3}, {k, 3}, {y, uPQ[[1]]}], 2],\n   Flatten[Table[Normal @ qmG[lS, lS, 1/3, -8/57][J, K][y], {J, subsetsA[2]}, {K, subsetsA[2]}, {y, uPQ[[2]]}], 2]];\ngenHelps = Not[And @@ Flatten @ Table[((om.O).nsT) === ConstantArray[0, Length[nsS]], {om, omsS}, {O, opsGen}]];\n\n(* (iii) the six polarized vacua (Weyl images) *)\nvacEigP[sig_][a_][w_][y_] := Sum[(Times @@ w[[sig[[II]]]]) kapG[lS, lS, 1/3, -8/57][II][y], {II, subsetsA[a]}];\nomegaP[sig_, w_] := omegaP[sig, w] = Module[{ch = chiOf[w], X},\n    X = Sum[Prime[10 + 7 a + 3 p] (Normal @ tauG[lS, lS, 1/3, -8/57][a, ch][uPQ[[a]][[p]]]\n        - vacEigP[sig][a][w][uPQ[[a]][[p]]] IdentityMatrix[dS]), {a, {1, 2}}, {p, Length[uPQ[[a]]]}];\n    NullSpace[Transpose[X]]];\npermDims = Table[Length[omegaP[sig, wSS[[1]]]], {sig, Permutations[Range[3]]}];\npermHelps = Not[And @@ Flatten @ Table[((First[omegaP[sig, w]].O).nsT) === ConstantArray[0, Length[nsS]],\n    {sig, Permutations[Range[3]]}, {w, wSS[[1 ;; 8]]}, {O, opS}]];\n\nGrid[{\n  {\"[3,0,0]^2, dim\", dS},\n  {\"dim W^perp with one companion insertion\", Length[nsS]},\n  {Style[\"(i) rank with k <= 1, 2, 3 insertions\", Bold], Style[kLadder, Bold]},\n  {\"    rule predicts (lam_1 >= 6-k)\", {63, 90, 100}},\n  {\"(ii) general non-companion twist reaches anything new\", genHelps},\n  {\"(iii) null-space dims of the 6 polarized vacua\", permDims},\n  {\"(iii) other polarized vacua reach anything new\", permHelps}\n }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"773602\" data-output-id=\"42\" data-out-n=\"92\" data-sub-idx=\"23\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"26\" data-sub-start=\"37\" data-sub-end=\"45\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[92]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:8.44em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:8.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">[3,0,0]</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">2, dim</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">dim W</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">perp with one companion insertion</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(i) rank with k &lt;= 1, 2, 3 insertions</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\"> rule predicts (lam_1 &gt;= 6-k)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(ii) general non-companion twist reaches anything new</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(iii) null-space dims of the 6 polarized vacua</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:0.59em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(iii) other polarized vacua reach anything new</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:8.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">100</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">37</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">63</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">90</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">100</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">63</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">90</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">False</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:0.59em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">False</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:8.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-10.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
