  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 12. Why: `adj (+) 1` tensor operators acting on a top-level seed\n\nThe `lambda_1` rule is not an accident. Two facts, both checked below, imply it.\n\n**(1) `tau_1` and `tau_2` are `adj (+) 1` tensor operators of the DIAGONAL `gl(3)`, for every twist and every `u`.** The quantum minors `qmin_{I,K}(u)` with `|I| = |K| = a` transform in `Lam^a(C^3) (x) Lam^a(C^3)*`. For `a = 1` that is `3 (x) 3bar = adj (+) 1`. For `a = 2`, `Lam^2(C^3) = C^3* (x) det`, so it is `3bar (x) 3 = adj (+) 1` **again** — the determinants of `det` cancel. For `a = 3` it is `1 (x) 1`, a pure singlet, which is exactly why `tau_3` is a multiple of the identity. A twist only chooses *which element* of that fixed 9-dimensional module you take; it cannot leave it. That is why a general non-companion twist buys nothing (§11(ii)).\n\nThe singlet inside the `a = 1` module is `Sum_i T_ii(u)`, the **untwisted** transfer matrix — `gl(3)`-invariant, as it must be.\n\n**(2) `<Om(w)|` lies entirely in the TOP `lambda_1` isotypic level.** Equivalently it is a left eigencovector of the quadratic Casimir with the top eigenvalue (for `[3,0,0]^2`, `C_2 = 48`, the component `(6,0,0)`), or for `adj (x) adj` is annihilated by `(C_2 - 28)(C_2 - 24)`, the two components at `lambda_1 = 4`. And **all six polarized vacua are top-level too** — which is exactly why none of them helps.\n\n**Conclusion.** By Wigner–Eckart an `adj (+) 1` operator connects `V_mu` to `V_nu` only when `nu - mu` is a root or zero. The roots of `gl(3)` are `e_i - e_j`, so one insertion shifts `lambda_1` by at most **one**. Starting from a top-level seed, `k` insertions reach `lambda_1 >= lamA_1 + lamB_1 - k`. That is the rule, and it is why the `adj (x) adj` singlet `(2,2,2)` dies: it sits at `lambda_1 = 2`, **two** root steps below `lambda_1 = 4`, so one insertion cannot reach it while two can.\n\n**What is still not explained.** The per-twist rank is 9, which equals `dim(adj (+) 1)`, but that identification is *not* established: a single 9-dimensional module applied to `<Om(w)|` gives only **4** (the same as `gl(3)` itself does), and it takes the union over all `a`, `y`, `u` to reach 9.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 12a. The two facts behind the rule. ---- *)\nClearAll[adClose, invCount];\nadClose[mats_, d_] := Module[{cur, new, k = 0},\n   cur = Select[RowReduce[Flatten /@ mats], AnyTrue[#, # =!= 0 &] &];\n   While[k < 4,\n    new = Join[cur, Flatten[Table[Flatten[Etot[i, j].ArrayReshape[v, {d, d}] - ArrayReshape[v, {d, d}].Etot[i, j]],\n        {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {v, cur}], 2]];\n    new = Select[RowReduce[new], AnyTrue[#, # =!= 0 &] &];\n    If[Length[new] == Length[cur], Break[]]; cur = new; k++];\n   cur];\ninvCount[mod_, d_] := Length @ NullSpace @ Transpose @ Table[\n    Flatten @ Table[Flatten[Etot[i, j].ArrayReshape[v, {d, d}] - ArrayReshape[v, {d, d}].Etot[i, j]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}],\n    {v, mod}];\n\n(* (1) the modules, on adj (x) adj *)\nmodT1 = adClose[Flatten[Table[Normal @ qminM[{i}, {k}][11/4], {i, 3}, {k, 3}], 1], 64];\nmodT2 = adClose[Flatten[Table[Normal @ qminM[J, K][11/4], {J, subsetsA[2]}, {K, subsetsA[2]}], 1], 64];\ntrTu = Flatten[Normal @ Sum[qminM[{i}, {i}][11/4], {i, 3}]];\n\n(* (2) the seed, on adj (x) adj and on [3,0,0]^2 *)\nc2A = Normal @ Sum[Etot[i, j].Etot[j, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\nomsA = Table[First @ omegaG[{2, 1, 0}, {2, 1, 0}, 1/3, -8/57, uPQ][w], {w, wSS}];\ntopA = And @@ Table[om.(c2A - 28 IdentityMatrix[64]).(c2A - 24 IdentityMatrix[64]) === ConstantArray[0, 64], {om, omsA}];\nc2S = Normal @ Sum[EtG[lS, lS][i, j].EtG[lS, lS][j, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\ntopS = And @@ Table[om.c2S === 48 om, {om, omsS}];\ntopSperm = And @@ Flatten @ Table[With[{om = First[omegaP[sig, w]]}, om.c2S === 48 om],\n    {sig, Permutations[Range[3]]}, {w, wSS[[1 ;; 8]]}];\n\nGrid[{\n  {Style[\"(1) tensor-operator structure\", Bold], \"\"},\n  {\"dim of the gl(3) module generated by the 9 T_ij(u)\", Length[modT1]},\n  {\"   number of gl(3) invariants in it (adj+1 => 1)\", invCount[modT1, 64]},\n  {\"   its singlet is the untwisted Sum_i T_ii(u)\", MatrixRank[Append[modT1, trTu]] == Length[modT1]},\n  {\"dim of the module generated by the 9 qmin_{I,K}(u), |I|=2\", Length[modT2]},\n  {\"   number of gl(3) invariants in it\", invCount[modT2, 64]},\n  {Style[\"(2) the seed is top-level\", Bold], \"\"},\n  {\"adj^2: <Om(w)| killed by (C2-28)(C2-24)\", topA},\n  {\"[3,0,0]^2: <Om(w)| is a C2 eigencovector, eigenvalue 48\", topS},\n  {\"[3,0,0]^2: ALL SIX polarized vacua likewise\", topSperm},\n  {Style[\"caveat\", Bold], \"one module on <Om(w)| gives only 4, not 9\"},\n  {\"<Om|.(T-module) / .(qmin-module) / both\",\n   {MatrixRank[Table[omsA[[1]].ArrayReshape[v, {64, 64}], {v, modT1}]],\n    MatrixRank[Table[omsA[[1]].ArrayReshape[v, {64, 64}], {v, modT2}]],\n    MatrixRank[Join[Table[omsA[[1]].ArrayReshape[v, {64, 64}], {v, modT1}], Table[omsA[[1]].ArrayReshape[v, {64, 64}], {v, modT2}]]]}}\n }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"773602\" data-output-id=\"44\" data-out-n=\"113\" data-sub-idx=\"15\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"28\" data-sub-start=\"28\" data-sub-end=\"44\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[113]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:14.44em;vertical-align:-6.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:14.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-6.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(1) tensor-operator structure</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">dim of the gl(3) module generated by the 9 T_ij(u)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\"> number of gl(3) invariants in it (adj+1 =&gt; 1)</span>