lass=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:14.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-6.95em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-10.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-12.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-13.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-14.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-15.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-16.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[113]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\mathbf{\\text{(1) tensor-operator structure}} & \\\\\\hline\\text{dim of the gl(3) module generated by the 9 T\\_ij(u)} & 9\\\\\\hline\\text{   number of gl(3) invariants in it (adj+1 => 1)} & 1\\\\\\hline\\text{   its singlet is the untwisted Sum\\_i T\\_ii(u)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{dim of the module generated by the 9 qmin\\_\\{I,K\\}(u), |I|=2} & 9\\\\\\hline\\text{   number of gl(3) invariants in it} & 1\\\\\\hline\\mathbf{\\text{(2) the seed is top-level}} & \\\\\\hline\\text{adj\\^{}2: <Om(w)| killed by (C2-28)(C2-24)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,0,0]\\^{}2: <Om(w)| is a C2 eigencovector, eigenvalue 48} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,0,0]\\^{}2: ALL SIX polarized vacua likewise} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\mathbf{\\text{caveat}} & \\text{one module on <Om(w)| gives only 4, not 9}\\\\\\hline\\text{<Om|.(T-module) / .(qmin-module) / both} & \\left\\{4,4,6\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "48f9c3f0-59a1-40e4-bd1f-f198a5928bc0"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 13. The cheap fix: one per-site rotation parameter\n\n### 13.1 The rule, sharpened\n\n`<Om(w)|` has support on **exactly one** isotypic component, `V_{lamA+lamB}` (the Cartan\ncomponent) — not merely on the top `lambda_1` level. So the correct statement is\n\n```\nW  =  V_{lamA+lamB}  (+)  (everything ONE ROOT STEP away),   with multiplicity\n```\n\nand the `lambda_1` formulation of §10 is a coarse shadow of it. Checked against all five cases:\n\n| `V1 (x) V2` | Cartan component + one root step | total | measured |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `[2,1,0](x)[1,0,0]` | `(3,1,0)15 + (2,2,0)6 + (2,1,1)3` | 24 | 24 |\n| `[2,1,0]^2` | `(4,2,0)27 + (4,1,1)10 + (3,3,0)10 + (3,2,1)16` | 63 | 63 |\n| `[3,0,0]^2` | `(6,0,0)28 + (5,1,0)35` | 63 | 63 |\n| `[3,1,0](x)[2,1,0]` | `(5,2,0)42 + (4,3,0)24 + (4,2,1)x2 30 + (5,1,1)15` | 111 | 111 |\n| `[3,1,0]^2` | `(6,2,0)60 + (6,1,1)21 + (5,3,0)42 + (5,2,1)x2 48` | 171 | 171 |\n\n### 13.2 Free covectors and where they sit\n\n| covector | isotypic support (adj^2) |\n|---|---|\n| `<hw (x) hw|`, `<lw (x) lw|`, `<Om(w)|` | Cartan component `(4,2,0)` only |\n| `<hw (x) lw|`, `<lw (x) hw|` | **every** component, singlet included |\n\nSo the vacuum is the *one* covector concentrated in a single component. That is the whole problem.\n\n### 13.3 The fix\n\nRotate the vacuum on **one site only**: `<Om(w)| (g1 (x) 1)`, `g1 = exp(c E^(1)_{31})`. This is an\nexponential of an adjoint tensor operator, so it takes arbitrarily many root steps and has full\nisotypic support. Measured on `adj (x) adj`, rank against the number of sampled `c` values:\n\n| # rotation parameters | 1 (`c = 0`) | 2 | 3 | 4 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| rank | 63 | **64** | 64 | 64 |\n\n**One nonzero `c` completes the space.** This is `O(1)` extra data, not `O(dim V)` as SoV would be,\nand `rotations/` §19 already established that per-site rotations **are** Q-determinants, so these\noverlaps are computable — which connects this directly to that thread.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 13a. Where free covectors sit, and the one-rotation-parameter fix. ---- *)\nClearAll[proj, support, pv, g1, seedRot];\nwts1 = Transpose[Table[Diagonal[JJ[i, i, {2, 1, 0}]], {i, 3}]];\nihw = First @ Flatten @ Position[wts1, {2, 1, 0}];\nilw = First @ Flatten @ Position[wts1, {0, 1, 2}];\npv[a_, b_] := UnitVector[64, (a - 1) 8 + b];\nc2A = Normal @ Sum[Etot[i, j].Etot[j, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\nc2ev = {28, 24, 18, 12};   (* (4,2,0) | (4,1,1)+(3,3,0) | (3,2,1)x2 | (2,2,2) *)\nproj[mu_] := proj[mu] = Fold[#1.(c2A - #2 IdentityMatrix[64])/(mu - #2) &, IdentityMatrix[64], DeleteCases[c2ev, mu]];\nsupport[v_] := Select[c2ev, v.proj[#] =!= ConstantArray[0, 64] &];\n\nomsA = Table[First @ omegaG[{2, 1, 0}, {2, 1, 0}, 1/3, -8/57, uPQ][w], {w, wSS}];\ng1[c_] := MatrixExp[c Normal[E1g[3, 1]]];   (* nilpotent, so exact *)\nseedRot[w_, c_] := First[omegaG[{2, 1, 0}, {2, 1, 0}, 1/3, -8/57, uPQ][w]].g1[c];\nopA33 = Table[Normal[opList[[k, 2]]], {k, Length[opList]}];\nrowsRot[nw_, cs_] := Join @@ Flatten[Table[Table[prim[seedRot[w, c].O], {O, opA33}], {w, wSS[[1 ;; nw]]}, {c, cs}], 1];\n\nGrid[{\n  {\"support of <hw (x) hw|\", support[pv[ihw, ihw]]},\n  {\"support of <lw (x) lw|\", support[pv[ilw, ilw]]},\n  {\"support of <Om(w)|\", support[omsA[[1]]]},\n  {Style[\"support of <hw (x) lw|\", Bold], Style[support[pv[ihw, ilw]], Bold]},\n  {Style[\"support of <lw (x) hw|\", Bold], Style[support[pv[ilw, ihw]], Bold]},\n  {\"support of the per-site-rotated vacuum\", support[seedRot[wSS[[1]], 5/7]]},\n  {Style[\"rank with 1, 2, 3, 4 rotation parameters (dim 64)\", Bold],\n   Style[{MatrixRank[rowsRot[8, {0}]], MatrixRank[rowsRot[8, {0, 5/7}]],\n          MatrixRank[rowsRot[8, {0, 5/7, -3/4}]], MatrixRank[rowsRot[8, {0, 5/7, -3/4, 2}]]}, Bold]}\n }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"773602\" data-output-id=\"45\" data-out-n=\"128\" data-sub-idx=\"15\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"30\" data-sub-start=\"17\" data-sub-end=\"27\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[128]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:8.44em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:8.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">support of &lt;hw (x) hw|</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">support of &lt;lw (x) lw|</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">support of &lt;Om(w)|</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span cla